{"name":"Jonquil","hex":"#eef293","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Jonquil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from English."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Jonquil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Narcissus jonquilla","blocks":[{"text":"Narcissus jonquilla, commonly known as jonquil or rush daffodil, is a bulbous flowering plant, a species of the genus Narcissus (daffodil) that is native to Spain and Portugal but has now become naturalised in many other regions: France, Italy, Turkey, the former Yugoslavia, Madeira, British Columbia in Canada, Utah, Illinois, Minnesota, Ohio, and the southeastern United States from Texas to Maryland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Narcissus_jonquilla_3.jpg/330px-Narcissus_jonquilla_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narcissus_jonquilla","wikidata":"Q1703489"},{"title":"Shades of yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color yellow may differ in hue, chroma or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a yellow or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Color_icon_yellow.svg/330px-Color_icon_yellow.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_yellow","wikidata":"Q7460348"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Narcissus_jonquilla_distrib.jpg/500px-Narcissus_jonquilla_distrib.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Narcissus_jonquilla_distrib.jpg/1280px-Narcissus_jonquilla_distrib.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam